natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Supernatural P.S. and P.E.", description: "The P.S. and P.E. of mutant bears are always considered supernatural, and most of their attacks do mega-damage. The bear itself is not a mega-damage creature: it has hit points, S.D.C. and a natural Armor Rating." }
  - { name: "Natural Armor Rating", description: "A.R. 10+1D6. An attacker must roll above the A.R. to inflict hit point/S.D.C. damage; mega-damage weapons automatically blast through an S.D.C. based A.R." }
  - { name: "Size and Build", description: "About 7 feet (2.1 m) tall and 700 to 900 pounds. An animal''s appearance with only a vaguely human, bipedal shape: a bear''s head, a fur covered body and a tiny tail. 85% have short legs, long powerful arms and a broad chest; 15% are more evenly proportioned and comparatively slender. Hands are only partially articulated, with an opposable thumb, short thick fingers and long claw-like nails. Stands and walks erect, though most (85%) run on all fours. Black Bears are 20% smaller; Brown Bears are 30% larger, Grizzly Bears 40% larger and Polar Bears 25% larger in height and weight." }
  - { name: "Bite", description: "By species. Black Bear: 6D6 S.D.C. (despite the supernatural P.S.). Brown Bear: 1D4 M.D. Grizzly Bear: 1D6 M.D. Polar Bear: 1D4 M.D." }
  - { name: "Sense Psychic and Magic Energy", description: "The Dog Boy''s ability, less developed: a constant, automatic sense for fellow psychics (I.S.P.) and for magic energy (P.P.E. spent as a spell, held in magic devices, or in people in large amounts of 80 points or more), followed like a scent to its source while the energy keeps being spent. Base Skill: 20% +5% per level of experience (roll once every melee round); halved when multiple sources are scattered throughout the sensing range. Range: 20 feet (printed as 12 m) +5 feet (1.5 m) per additional level for a psychic or magic practitioner NOT using his powers; 200 feet (61 m) +20 feet (6 m) per level for psionic and magic powers being used. Roll every 400 feet (122 m) to stay on the trail; a failed roll means the scent is lost. I.S.P.: none, automatic. Cannot Recognize Psychic Scent." }
  - { name: "Sense Supernatural Beings", description: "The Dog Boy''s ability, less acute: works like Sense Psychic and Magic Energy, tuned to the distinctive psychic scent of the supernatural. Base Skill: 40% +2% per level to identify the specific type/race of paranormal creature (alien intelligences, gods, demigods, demons, vampires and dragons included) and to detect whether a person is possessed. Tracking by this scent: 15% +5% per level, or 53% +3% per level if the being is also using psionics or magic. Range: 100 feet (30.5 m) per level when the being is using no special, magical or psionic powers; 1000 feet (305 m) +100 feet (30.5 m) per additional level when it is actively using them. Automatic and constant, no I.S.P. Close proximity to ley lines and nexus points disrupts the psychic senses." }
  - { name: "Sense of Smell", description: "A third to half as keen as a Dog Boy''s but 10 times better than a human''s. Common and strong scents (gases, food, animals, the path of a group, other distinctive odors): 43% +3% per level, range 100 feet (30.5 m) per level. Identify specific odors (a specific individual, poison or drugs in food or drink, unusual scents; needs familiarity with the subject or a reference such as clothing, hair or blood): 26% +2% per level, range 25 feet (7.6 m) per level. Track by smell alone: 20% +4% per level; can sniff a way through total darkness and suffers only HALF the normal penalties to strike, parry and dodge when blinded or in darkness. Roll once per 500 feet (152 m), half that if the scent is light or under light rain or snow; a failed roll loses the trail temporarily, two successes in three tries recover it, two failures lose it. Follows a scent up to a day (24 hours) old. Cannot track through water, nor smell Astral Beings, ghosts or energy beings." }
  - { name: "Other Senses", description: "Hearing only a little better than a human''s. Taste and vision about the same as a canine''s, with a 200 degree field of vision. Sees in the dark only about 30% better than a human. Black Bears have Nightvision 200 feet (61 m)." }
  - { name: "Sprinter", description: "Can run at double normal speed for 1D4 minutes before dropping back to normal speed. Digging speed is 2D4." }
  - { name: "Polar Bear Traits", description: "Polar Bears only: a natural, expert swimmer (96%) who can hold breath underwater for six minutes and dive 20 feet (6 m), and is resistant to cold (cold does half damage); dense fur keeps it warm at -40 degrees Fahrenheit." }
  - { name: "Sensitivity to Ley Line Energy", description: "Ley lines and nexus points obliterate the psychic and supernatural sensing abilities and give the bear a headache, so they cannot be used on a ley line or near a nexus; the physical senses are unaffected and the other psychic abilities are enhanced as usual. Ley Line Storms cause physical discomfort (headaches, crackling in the ears, static shocks) and the bear is two times more likely to be struck by ley line energy and lightning." }
  - { name: "Temperament", description: "Most have the mental capacity, attention span and emotional maturity of a 7 to 10 year old child and follow the mood and lead of their comrades. In danger, or when comrades are endangered, the bear flies into an aggressive frenzy that can become a berserker rage like a Kill Hound''s, usually only when comrades are near destruction or have fallen, or when cornered and alone. Human speech is partial and guttural. Black Bears love sweets, especially honey and chocolate. Matures at the same basic rate as a Dog Boy; life span an estimated 30 to 45 years." }
