extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 72-75 (cache p073-p076, cache page = printed folio + 1; printed 73 is a full-page illustration and its cache page is empty). Every number was read off renders of cache p073, p075 and p076. || XP: the column headed Ursa-Warrior (Bear) at the foot of printed 174 (cache p175), read off the render, lower bound of each band. || HEADING: Ursa-Warrior R.C.C., under Mutant Bears; a race. || ATTRIBUTES as printed (Average Attribute Range, Standard Ursa-Warrior): I.Q. 2D6, M.E. 2D6, M.A. 2D6, P.S. 5D6, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 4D6, P.B. 2D6, Spd 4D6 running; 2D4 digging is in the Sprinter ability text. || POOLS: Hit points P.E. x5 plus 2D6 per level. S.D.C. is printed as ''P.E. attribute number plus 2D4x10 plus those gained from physical skills; some species get S.D.C. bonuses''. Stored as sdc_base ''P.E. + 2d4x10'' and NOT as bonuses.pools.sdc (judgement, against the usual racial-pool reading): the printed base contains the P.E. attribute, which a pool bonus of a number or one dice expression cannot carry, and bonuses.pools.sdc is where each species variant states its printed extra S.D.C. (Brown +1D6x10, Grizzly +2D4x10, Polar +1D6x10), so the base and the species bonus are two separate printed figures. Because sdc_base is stated there is no men_of_arms line. P.P.E. 3D6. A.R. 10+1D6 is a natural ability text. || SPECIES (Physical Bonuses, printed 74): the four species are four variants; the class with no variant is the printed Standard Ursa-Warrior with no species bonus. A variant''s bonuses block restates the +1 save vs psionic attack and mind control that every bear has. Attribute bonuses are stored as bonuses.attributes (dice strings) rather than folded into attribute_dice. Black Bear: +1 initiative, +1 strike and parry, +3 vs disease, +3 vs horror factor, I.Q. +1D4, M.A. +1D6, P.P. +1D6, Spd +3D6, Climbing +20% (60+20 = 80); size -20%, Nightvision 200 ft, bite 6D6 S.D.C. as text. Brown Bear: +3 initiative, +2 strike and parry, +4 disease, +6 horror factor, +5D6 hit points, +1D6x10 S.D.C., I.Q. +1, P.S. +2D6, P.E. +1D6, Spd +2D6, Wrestling granted; size +30%, bite 1D4 M.D. as text. Grizzly Bear: +2 initiative, +3 strike, +2 parry, +1 attack, +4 disease, +8 horror factor, +1D6x10 hit points, +2D4x10 S.D.C., P.S. +3D6, P.E. +2D6, Swimming +10% (60), Climbing -10% (50); size +40%, bite 1D6 M.D. as text. Polar Bear: +3 initiative, +4 strike, +1 parry and dodge, +1 attack, +4 disease, +7 horror factor, +1D4x10 hit points, +1D6x10 S.D.C., I.Q. +1D6, P.S. +3D6, P.E. +2D6, Spd +2D6, Swimming 96%; breath-holding, diving and cold resistance, size +25%, bite 1D4 M.D. as text. The horror factor figures are SAVES vs horror factor; the book prints no horror factor the bear projects. || PSIONICS: ''effectively major psionics'', saves on 12 or higher, +1 vs psionic attack and all forms of mind control (saves.psionics and saves.mind_control). Two powers from the Physical category and no later picks printed. I.S.P. is M.E. doubled, plus 2D4 per each ADDITIONAL level; regained at two per hour of activity or eight per hour of meditation or sleep. The two sensing abilities are natural abilities text; the book says ''same as the Dog Boys but not as developed'' and prints its own numbers, and the description of what the sense does is restated from the Dog Boy entry on printed 33. The book prints the non-use range as ''20 feet (12 m)''; the metric figure is the book''s. || SKILLS: Speaks American at 80% is Language: Native Tongue 80, per_level 0. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Land Navigation 36+10 = 46. Wilderness Survival 30+15 = 45. W.P. Heavy Energy is the catalog''s W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons. Hand to Hand: Expert with no upgrade price printed, so no hand_to_hand block. Natural climbers 60%/40% and natural swimmers 50% are stored as Climbing 60 and Swimming 50 with the catalog''s 5% per level (judgement: the book prints a base skill and no per-level step); the second climbing figure, 40%, is in the skill note. || RELATED: four at level one, plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. Domestic +5, Medical (First Aid only) +5, Pilot (Hovercraft, Truck, sail and motorboat only) +5, Technical +5, Wilderness +10; Electrical and Science none. Motorboat is Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil and sail is Boat: Sail Type. Pick Locks and Pick Pockets at half proficiency is in the note; the catalog files both under Espionage, which the class takes as Any. ''Never taught to read'' applies to bears in CS service and is a restriction line, not an exclusion. SECONDARY: four at level one plus one at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, same lists without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the large 50 M.D.C. riot suit is the dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor row, with the printed 50 M.D.C. in the item note. Radio as walkie-talkie; 100 ft of lightweight rope as five 20 ft lengths; four spikes; a pair of Vibro-Knives or Vibro-Claws as a choice at qty 2; two gallon-size canteens as canteen x2. The printed comb is not stored: it has no catalog row and is a trivial personal item. The Vibro-Saber or Neuro-Mace many also have, the uniform, shorts or jumpsuit and collar, and the equipment available upon assignment (energy weapons, rail gun, heavy weapons, grenades, flares, light vehicle, rations) are not stored. || MONEY: the book prints no starting sum, only a token monthly salary of 60-100 credits with all basic needs provided by the CS military; no starting_money stored. || Identification coding (the Dog Boys'' dual I.D. system), typical missions and the deployment numbers are lore."
---

## Lore

The Ursa-Warrior is the Lone Star complex''s attempt to add raw muscle to the
Dog Pack. Its makers started from bear stock, a distant relative of the dog,
and spliced in canine traits for loyalty and group living. Black and polar
bear lines took to squad life well; grizzly and brown bear lines stayed more
aggressive and harder to trust.

Most of these mutants are slow, easily distracted and childlike, happiest in a
small squad of friends under a leader they trust, and they mirror the mood of
whoever is around them. Left unsupervised they drift into mischief: wandering
off post, raiding the sweets, napping on duty. Attempts to raise their
intelligence have so far cost the very sociability the program wanted, turning
out cunning, rebellious loners instead.

Only a handful exist. They serve one to a squad as heavy-weapon carriers and
pack mules, share a weaker version of the Dog Boy''s psychic nose, and are
treated as test animals under observation rather than as soldiers.

## GM Notes

Pick a species at creation: the four species differ widely in combat bonuses,
hit points and S.D.C., and the standard block alone is the bare average. The
bear''s strength and endurance are supernatural, so its blows do mega-damage,
but the bear itself is an S.D.C. creature with a natural Armor Rating that
mega-damage weapons ignore.

The Dog Boy optional tables are closed to bears; only the Mutation Gone Wrong
table may be used, and only with the G.M.''s approval. A bear outside Coalition
service is a feral or a free-born and is killed on sight by the CS.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ursa-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ursa-warrior';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-ursa-warrior-class.sql');
